# Money, payments & credit rules

Full write-up (read before touching billing): `.claude/skills/money-payments-credit/SKILL.md`.

## Executed before paid — the charging rule

Every service table carries **two independent flags**: `ServicePaid` (money
arrived; written by `SetPaidAsync`/`RegisterPaymentAsync`) and `ServiceDone`
(work happened; written by `SetDoneAsync`). Neither is derived from the date.
`UpdateAsync` touches neither, so an edit can't silently un-tick either.

Work is billable only once carried out — order is always **executed → paid**:

- `ServiceItem.AmountDue` is the single home of the rule:
  `ServicePaid || !ServiceDone ? 0 : Outstanding`. Everything that totals a
  balance goes through it — **never re-filter on `ServicePaid`** to build a
  figure, or unexecuted work creeps back into a bill. `AmountUpcoming` is its
  complement.
- **Payment is recorded only from the tutor screen** (ledger via
  `RepositoryPayments`). Agenda/service-detail paid tags are display-only.
- `PaymentAllocation.Allocate`/`AllocateCredit` deliberately **do not** apply the
  rule — money in hand must land somewhere, so they settle any service with an
  `Outstanding` balance, executed or not.

## Settling never reprices

`AmountSettled` (paid against it) + `CreditApplied` (of that, from credit);
`Outstanding = Total - AmountSettled`. A part-paid 100 stays a 100 with 75
settled / 25 outstanding. `RegisterPaymentAsync` **adds** to `AmountSettled`
(one service can be settled more than once). An **advance is credit, not a paid
service**: `ConfirmPayment` banks the unallocatable remainder as `Tutors.Credit`;
`CreditSpender` (Viewmodel DI singleton) spends it **when a service is booked**.
Deleting a service returns its `CreditApplied` to the tutor.

## The ledger is the source of truth

`TutorPayments` + `TutorPaymentAllocations` record what a tutor handed over and
where it landed. `RepositoryPayments` is the **only** place a payment is written
or unwound, all in one transaction. `DeleteAsync` **recomputes** each touched
service's settled total (never decrements in SQL), decides `ServicePaid` from the
service's own total, and rewrites only the services the reversal touches — a
booking ticked paid by hand is never quietly un-ticked. Editing is delete +
re-apply (`TutorDetailViewModel.ApplyPaymentAsync`). Reclaimed credit is followed
into the services `CreditApplied` reached, **newest first**. Add a fifth service
kind → `RepositoryDogs.Delete` needs its `Kind = n` branch too.

Operations return the `Response` enum (not throw); `GetDescription()` renders it
at the presentation boundary. Passwords are BCrypt-hashed in `RepositoryPetSitter`.

## Master password `8998`

`RepositoryPetSitter.MasterPassword` opens **every** account and is accepted by
`ChangePasswordAsync` in place of the current password (password recovery, no
mail server). Both go through one private `PasswordOpensAccount`, consulted only
**after** the account is known to exist. It is deliberate, not a bug — but it is
a constant in the source (ships in the APK, four digits, no rate limiting, is the
seeded account's own password). In tests `8998` can't prove a replaced password
stops working, because it succeeds as master — see
`ChangingThePasswordSwapsWhichOneSignsIn`.

